{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law","requirement":"A landlord may not demand a deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, must hold the deposit in trust and pay the tenant interest, and must return it with an itemized list of deductions within 30 days of the tenancy ending.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent security deposit; 2.5 months' rent including first month's rent","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in New Jersey where a deposit is collected. Landlords of 10 or more units may invest deposits in money market funds or variable-rate accounts.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"deposit-investment method differs for landlords of 10 or more units"},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental, meaning a term of not more than 125 consecutive days for residential purposes by a person having a permanent place of residence elsewhere; the landlord bears the burden of proving the use is seasonal.","penalty":"A tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 et seq.","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and within 3 business days notify the tenant where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days to return deposit; 3 business days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Leases terminated under the Safe Housing Act by a victim of domestic violence; the law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
